Each pair is the 90% block-bootstrap interval for that pillar's
learned weight. The simplex constrains weights to [0,1] summing to
1, so an interval spanning most of [0,1] means the weight is not an
estimate of anything and two-decimal reporting would be false
precision. L=770 is the measured integral timescale; shorter
lengths understate dependence and so understate the width.

